<InfoPanel Title="Prototype Boundary Checklist" Subtitle="Clear boundaries stop reviewers from confusing the portfolio prototype with a full production deployment.">
    <div class="of-two-column-grid">
        <GuidanceNote Title="What this prototype does" Icon="✅" Tone="success">
            <ul>
                <li>Runs as a local Blazor/SQLite demo app.</li>
                <li>Tracks workflow metadata across multiple modules.</li>
                <li>Creates and edits key workflow records.</li>
                <li>Shows traceability through activity history and Activity Log.</li>
                <li>Exports demo data to CSV files.</li>
                <li>Demonstrates Microsoft 365-ready workflow thinking.</li>
            </ul>
        </GuidanceNote>

        <GuidanceNote Title="What this prototype does not yet do" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
            <ul>
                <li>Does not use live authentication or role-based permissions yet.</li>
                <li>Does not sync to Microsoft Lists or SharePoint yet.</li>
                <li>Does not send live Teams or Outlook notifications yet.</li>
                <li>Does not store real production business documents.</li>
                <li>Does not enforce production audit retention rules yet.</li>
                <li>Does not replace a full ERP, job management, or safety platform.</li>
            </ul>
        </GuidanceNote>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<InfoPanel Title="Week 3 / Week 4 Forward Path" Subtitle="What the next implementation stage should prove.">
    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <strong>Week 3</strong>
            <span>Hybrid implementation foundation: map local prototype data to Microsoft Lists/SharePoint-ready structures while keeping the app useful without a tenant.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <strong>Week 4</strong>
            <span>Microsoft 365 implementation: use a test tenant to build live Microsoft Lists, Power Automate flows, Teams/Outlook notifications, and Power BI-style reporting.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <strong>Portfolio</strong>
            <span>Business systems proof: show the same thinking used in real-world AIE automation, including intake, routing, ownership, follow-up, reporting, and traceability.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <strong>Polish</strong>
            <span>Final cleanup pass: clean CSS, spacing, mobile behaviour, screenshots, README, and demo flow once functionality is locked.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>